    "text": "He spent 1*25%=25% less time on research than his acclimation period so he spent 25/75*100% = 33.33% less time on research\nThat means he spent 1-33.33% = 66.67% as much time on research\nSo he spent 2*66.67% = 13.33% less time on research\nThat means he spent 1-13.33% = 86.67% as much time on research\nSo he spent 2*86.67% = 173.33% as much time on research\nThat means he spent 173.33% / 100% = 1.7333 times as much time on research\nSo he spent 1+1.7333 = 2.7333 times as much time on everything\nSo he spent 1+2.7333 = 3.7333 years on everything\nThe final answer is \\boxed{3.7333}.",
